From 7c043f488b68c9a033cad21a394ec8598378475a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:32:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] feat: cost-model admission for disk 'shorter' matches
 (Phase M2 lever 1, revised)

Replaces the fixed 1500-token admission constant with online EWMA
estimates of this process's own prefill tokens/s (timed from the
progress callback, prefill only, excludes decode) and disk read MB/s
(timed inside DiskPromptStore.load()). A 'shorter' match is admitted
only when its estimated prefill-time savings clear its estimated
read-time cost by a configurable safety factor
(--prompt-cache-disk-admission-safety-factor, default 1.5). A fixed
token count's break-even point is itself a function of host/model/disk
speed, so it silently stops being correct anywhere else; this
self-calibrates from observed traffic instead.
---
 mlx_lm/prompt_cache_disk.py     | 81 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 mlx_lm/server.py                | 37 +++++++++++----
 tests/test_prompt_cache_disk.py | 58 +++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 137 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

